.TH SDL_RenderDebugText 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_RenderDebugText \- Draw debug text to an
.BR SDL_Renderer .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_RenderDebugText(SDL_Renderer *renderer, float x, float y, const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will render a string of text to an
.BR SDL_Renderer \[char46]
Note that this is a convenience function for debugging, with severe limitations, and not intended to be used for production apps and games\[char46]
.PP
Among these limitations:
.PP

\(bu It accepts UTF-8 strings, but will only renders ASCII characters\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It has a single, tiny size (8x8 pixels)\[char46] You can use logical presentation or
.BR SDL_SetRenderScale ()
to adjust it\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It uses a simple, hardcoded bitmap font\[char46] It does not allow different font selections and it does not support truetype, for proper scaling\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It does no word-wrapping and does not treat newline characters as a line break\[char46] If the text goes out of the window, it\(aqs gone\[char46]
.PP
For serious text rendering, there are several good options, such as
.BR SDL_ttf ,
stb_truetype, or other external libraries\[char46]
.PP
On first use, this will create an internal texture for rendering glyphs\[char46] This texture will live until the renderer is destroyed\[char46]
.PP
The text is drawn in the color specified by
.BR SDL_SetRenderDrawColor ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the renderer which should draw a line of text\[char46]
.TP
.I x
the x coordinate where the top-left corner of the text will draw\[char46]
.TP
.I y
the y coordinate where the top-left corner of the text will draw\[char46]
.TP
.I str
the string to render\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_RenderDebugTextFormat (3),
.BR SDL_DEBUG_TEXT_FONT_CHARACTER_SIZE (3)
